1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,370
Remind me, Trevor... how long is the presentation?

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:05,860
Dr White said three per hour.

3
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:07,820
So about twenty minutes?

4
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:10,860
Well... it'll be fifteen minutes per presentation.

5
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,820
And five minutes for questions.

6
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:15,530
And is this one going to be assessed?

7
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:19,690
No... not this time round... because it's the first one... you know.

8
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:21,050
Good news.

9
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:24,500
Well, Trevor, what are we going to include?

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,940
Well... Do you think we ought to give some historical background?

11
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:30,880
Oh no... definitely not... we won't have time!

12
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:34,975
OK... but I think we ought to say something about the geographical location...

13
00:00:34,975 --> 00:00:38,440
cos not a lot of people know where the islands are...

14
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:42,060
Yes... OK... I'll take notes, shall I?

15
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,760
Yeah, that'll be a help...

16
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:48,630
So... geographical location...

17
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:52,240
Then we ought to give an overview of the whole education system.

18
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:55,940
Shouldn't we say something about the economy... you know

19
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:58,840
agricultural produce... minerals and so forth?

20
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:02,650
Well... Dr White said we shouldn't go into that sort of detail.

21
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:05,400
But it's pretty important when you think about it...

22
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,150
you know because it does influence the education system...

23
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:10,700
Look... let's think about that one later shall we

24
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:12,530
Let's see how we're doing for time...

25
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:19,360
OK... so... general overview of education Of course

26
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,050
and then the role of English language...

27
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:26,130
Nope... that goes in the Language Policy Seminar... don't you remember?

28
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,170
Are you sure?

29
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,160
Positive.

30
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:33,470
All right... so those are the topics we're going to be... to be covering...

31
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:35,806
We need to think about what to prepare...

32
00:01:35,806 --> 00:01:39,019
Dr White said he wanted us to use plenty of visuals

33
00:01:39,019 --> 00:01:43,400
and things and we might as well try them out when we're not being assessed...

34
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,510
Well, the most important thing is the overhead projector...

35
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:50,670
No problem... we'll get that from the media room... must remember to book it...

36
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:53,320
Well... we'll need a map of course.

37
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:57,290
Probably two... one of the islands... large scale.

38
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:58,600
And one of West Africa.

39
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,820
Well, the West African one is no problem... There's one in the Resources Room.

40
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:04,880
Oh yeah, of course, the resources room

41
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:08,110
the islands are going to be more of a problem.

42
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:15,370
Tell you what... there's a very clear map of Santiago in that tourist brochure I showed you last week. Don't you remember it?

43
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:19,490
Oh yeah... that's right; we can just use the tourist brochure.

44
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:23,600
We also need statistics... on several different things.

45
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,800
Literacy rates.

46
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,570
Yes, and school places.

47
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,060
How about the encyclopaedia?

48
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:30,440
Nah... not up-to-date enough!

49
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,160
Mmm... why don't we call the embassy?

50
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,700
Oh... someone's enthusiastic!

51
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,800
Well... if something's worth doing...

52
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,660
I know, it's worth doing well... OK.

53
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:44,420
We can find out statistics on school places from them as well.

54
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:45,710
Might as well.

55
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:48,246
Look, Julie, it's almost time for our tutorials...

56
00:02:48,246 --> 00:02:53,000
we can meet again on Monday... but we need to prepare some stuff before then...
